A top-level :INCLUDE placed after a :DECLARE. include_early is info tier,
so it appears only under --info (diag.include_early first Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;
:INCLUDE Common.StringHelpers;
nCount := 0;
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount;
:INCLUDE Common.StringHelpers;
nCount := 0;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:1-2:9 info include_early: ':INCLUDE' should appear early in the file. Recommended order: :PARAMETERS, :DEFAULT, :INCLUDE, :PUBLIC, :DECLARE
